      "standard_prerequisites": [],
      "core_obligations": [
        "Beyond prior Gauss-Weingarten and Mainardi-Codazzi identities, the author constructs a vector conservation potential and two pseudospherical surfaces; conversely the equal-curvature parallelism forces a unimodular mapping tensor, Peterson eigendirections and signed asymptotic directions on the middle surface. The proof must select the two admissible sign pairs, handle the nondegeneracy restriction and show both concordance and Chebyshev Christoffel cancellation. This is one bidirectional geometric correspondence, not separate counts for explicit coordinate checks."
      ],
      "proof_roadmap": [
        "Full original article mathematical body, examples, appendix, figures and inline bibliography retained; counted primary is the two directions of the local correspondence. Local genericity and net versus parametrisation distinction (1806-1809) preserved."
